# What never enters a build context.
#
# The first block keeps `.env` out of the build
# context. A file that is not sent cannot be COPYed in by accident, cannot end
# up in a layer, and cannot be read out of the image afterwards — which is what
# makes this stronger than "we do not copy it".
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Installed and generated locally. They would be copied into the build only to
# be overwritten by the container's own install — and a host `node_modules`
# carries binaries built for the host, not for Alpine.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
**/dist/
build/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# History and CI metadata. The application version comes in as a build
# argument, so the image never needs the repository.
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Test output and local tooling state.
playwright-report/
test-results/
blob-report/
.playwright/
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/

# Documentation and specifications — several megabytes of design handoff that
# no image runs.
docs/
CHANGELOG.md
README.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md

# Only the two application Dockerfiles are ever used, and each is passed with
# `-f`; sending them along would just invalidate cache layers.
**/Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
